Alembic migrations for agent-props.

The schema itself is declared once, in ../sql.py, and env.py hands that
MetaData to Alembic as the autogenerate target. Nothing here restates a column.

    uv run alembic upgrade head    # apply
    uv run alembic check           # compare a live database against sql.py
    uv run alembic downgrade base  # drop it all again

The URL comes from AGENTPROPS_DB_URL, or from sqlalchemy.url in
../../../../alembic.ini, or from `-x url=...`.

Two indexes are Postgres-only, per docs/contracts.md section 7:
datasets_labels_gin and datasets_search. They are created by the initial
revision inside a dialect branch and excluded from autogenerate comparison by
env.py's include_object, so neither dialect reports drift.

tests/integration/test_migrations.py applies these to a fresh database and
asserts the result matches sql.py's MetaData table for table, column for
column, index for index. A migration nobody runs is not a migration.
